    <string name="help_quick_start_title">Quick start</string>
    <string name="help_quick_start_body">Import a profile from the clipboard, a file, or a QR code, select it as active, and tap Start.\n\nURL subscriptions are supported for compatible VPN configurations, including v2raytun-compatible node lists and smart profiles.</string>
    <string name="help_profiles_subscriptions_title">Profiles and subscriptions</string>
    <string name="help_profiles_subscriptions_body">Profiles store connection parameters: server, protocol, keys, routes, and tunnel settings.\n\nIn Profiles, you can choose the active profile, refresh a subscription, view or edit the configuration, and export the configuration.\n\nManual edits inside a subscription profile can be replaced by the next subscription refresh.\n\nRefresh is available for URL subscriptions. Foxhole downloads the latest configuration from the VPN provider. If the profile is already connected to the VPN tunnel, the app reconnects it to apply the changes.</string>
    <string name="help_smart_start_full_body">Smart start chooses a working VPN protocol for the current network.\n\nIt tries the best available protocols, validates the connection, and keeps the first confirmed result. Full refresh checks every available protocol separately and updates latency, status, and recommendations.\n\nSmart start data stays on the device: saved latency, statuses, recommendations, and connection history are not sent out.\n\nSmart start settings appear automatically after Foxhole detects a smart profile. In settings, you can change connection timeouts, choose the UDP / TCP / All transport priority, or clear local Smart start data.\n\nProtocol menu legend:\n\n★ Fast - the fastest successful option from saved measurements.\n\n★★ Best - the protocol Foxhole recommends for connection based on the latest checks.</string>
    <string name="help_protocol_statuses_title">Protocol statuses</string>
    <string name="help_protocol_statuses_body">Fast - latency up to 250 ms. Usually the best option for everyday connection.\n\nNormal - latency from 251 to 750 ms. The connection works, but may not be the fastest.\n\nSlow - latency from 751 to 1500 ms. The protocol works, but connection quality is lower.\n\nVery slow - latency above 1500 ms. Use it only when other options are unavailable.\n\nDown - the latest protocol check failed. This protocol should not appear as recommended after a fresh failed result.\n\nUnavailable - Foxhole could not get a valid latency or ping measurement for this protocol.\n\nNo data - analysis has not run yet, or there are no saved results for this protocol.\n\nOff - the protocol was turned off manually and does not participate in auto-connect until the user turns it back on.</string>
    <string name="help_connection_modes_title">Connection modes</string>
    <string name="help_connection_modes_body">Tunnel routes device traffic through the active profile. This is the main VPN mode. Reconnect after changing DNS, MTU, IPv6, or tunnel stack.\n\nSplit Tunnel lets you choose which apps use VPN and which bypass it. App rules work on top of the active profile.\n\nProxy starts local HTTP, SOCKS5, or Mixed endpoints for apps. Traffic goes through Foxhole only where the local proxy is configured explicitly.\n\nLAN Proxy exposes the proxy over Wi-Fi to other devices on the local network. Enable it only on a trusted Wi-Fi network. Without a Wi-Fi address, local-network connections are unavailable.</string>
    <string name="help_routing_full_body">Routing adds rules for apps, sites, domains, IP addresses, ports, and protocols.\n\nA preset can be created, imported, exported, enabled, or disabled. Catalogs help connect prepared rule sets.</string>
    <string name="help_dashboard_network_title">Network on the main screen</string>
    <string name="help_dashboard_network_body">The Network card shows the current public IP, country, city, and provider.\n\nAfter connection, the data should refresh through the VPN tunnel. Manual refresh starts a new network check.\n\nVPN latency, server ping, connection time, and status help evaluate connection quality.</string>
    <string name="help_traffic_usage_title">Traffic usage</string>
    <string name="help_traffic_usage_body">Statistics show incoming, outgoing, and total traffic for the current session.\n\nReset clears only the local counter on this device. It does not affect the profile, subscription, or active connection.</string>
    <string name="help_diagnostics_support_title">Diagnostics and support</string>
    <string name="help_diagnostics_support_body">Diagnostics shows connection logs, traffic statistics, and sanitized archive export.\n\nThe sanitized archive does not contain IP addresses or configurations. It is used to debug connection, import, subscription, and Smart start issues.\n\nIf the problem repeats, open Diagnostics, create a sanitized archive without IP addresses or configurations, and send it to the Telegram support bot.\n\nIf Telegram is not installed, Foxhole opens the link in a browser.</string>
    <string name="help_application_settings_body">This section contains theme, language, auto reconnect, auto start, screenshot protection, IP check, and the Android Quick Settings tile.\n\nThese settings change app behavior, but not the profile configuration.</string>
    <string name="help_expert_full_body">Expert settings change routing, DNS, local interfaces, import restrictions, and diagnostics.\n\nOpen them only if you understand the consequences or are following support instructions.\n\nTo open the section, tap the version card 5 times.</string>
    <string name="help_smart_start_body">Smart start connects quickly by trying only the best local candidates for the current network. Refresh checks all eligible protocols to update latency, status, and recommendations. All Smart start data stays on the device.</string>
    <string name="help_tunnel_body">Routes the whole device through the active profile.</string>
    <string name="help_split_tunnel_body">Lets selected apps use the VPN tunnel or bypass it, depending on the selected mode.</string>
    <string name="help_proxy_body">Starts local HTTP, SOCKS5, or Mixed endpoints for apps.</string>
    <string name="help_lan_proxy_body">Opens LAN Proxy over Wi-Fi so other devices on the local network can use the proxy through your phone. Enable it only when the phone is on a trusted Wi-Fi network.</string>
    <string name="help_profiles_body">Stores connection servers. You can import, switch, refresh, and edit them here.</string>
    <string name="help_routing_body">Adds local app and site rules on top of the active profile.</string>
    <string name="help_logs_body">Shows the connection log, traffic statistics, and anonymized diagnostics export.</string>
    <string name="help_expert_body">Open Settings and tap the version card 5 times to open this section.</string>
